00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.240
What is it exactly?

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:23.320
What is the difference with
others like Travis or Jenkins?

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.630
BRAD RYDZEWSKI: Sure, I think
the biggest difference is

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:28.000
that Drone is built
from the ground up

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.000
to use containers as the
build runtime, specifically,

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.710
right now, it uses Docker.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:36.910
So every single build and
build step executes in a Docker

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.910
container itself and
the configuration

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:43.240
is defined as a superset
of the Docker Compose Yml.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:46.027
So it's really a
container-first solution.

00:06:46.027 --> 00:06:48.610
MARK MANDEL: So this project,
is it open source, is it hosted?

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:49.975
What's the idea there?

00:06:49.975 --> 00:06:52.058
